The 2025 restriction adds an important dimension to the question of whether the Ombudsman was a practically accessible and effective pathway.
The issue is not simply whether the Ombudsman had statutory jurisdiction. It is whether I could realistically access that jurisdiction and obtain consideration of the substance of my concerns.
If a service restriction prevented consideration of genuinely new or materially different complaints, that practical effect is relevant to assessing access to justice.
The investigation should also consider whether reasonable adjustments, disability-related access requirements and alternative communication arrangements were available.
I do not ask that the restriction be presumed unlawful or retaliatory. I ask that its terms, reasons, legal basis and consequences be independently assessed.
