6. Did it examine my concerns about possible conflicts of interest?
7. Did it initiate an inquiry or investigation?
8. Did it obtain or request relevant documents?
9. Did it provide reasons for any decision not to investigate?
10. Was an independent alternative available if I believed the oversight process itself was compromised?
11. Was I informed of any review or reconsideration process?
I request that these questions be answered through examination of the actual IGIS records, not assumptions about the institutionâ€™s motives.
