The central issue is not simply that government offices referred my correspondence elsewhere.
It is whether those referrals resulted in an actual, independent examination of the matters raised.
A referral may be administratively appropriate in isolation but still fail to provide an effective remedy if the receiving institution declines the matter, lacks jurisdiction, imposes restrictions or does not address the substance of the complaint.
The chronology therefore raises questions about:
* The substantive assessment of my original correspondence.
* The reasons for the Prime Ministerâ€™s Officeâ€™s non-forwarding decision.
