* Whether any effective alternative mechanism was provided.
* Whether any institution took responsibility for coordinating or resolving the issues raised.
Administrative and human consequences
I describe the cumulative consequences I report experiencing as administrative burden, administrative harm, institutional betrayal and denial of access to justice.
These are analytical descriptions of the consequences of unresolved complaints and procedural barriers. They are not findings of criminal intent by any particular officeholder or institution.
The wider significance is that repeated administrative referrals may impose an additional burden on a person who is already seeking protection, accountability and a substantive response.
The assessment should therefore consider not only whether each individual office followed an administrative process, but whether the combined process provided an effective and accessible means of obtaining independent scrutiny.
